[TEXT] All the evidence is now in hand. Let me compile the findings:

- **r1.startup** defines 10 `MASQUERADE` rules (one per internal subnet × two ISP uplinks) in Section D
- **Live iptables** has **zero MASQUERADE/SNAT rules** in the POSTROUTING chain — all were stripped out
- **r1 can ping both ISPA (203.0.113.1) and ISPB (203.0.113.5)** — the ISP circuits are 100% healthy
